  "releaseNotes": "- [Vulkan] HeapRenderObjectCommand: recompile now RESETS the previous generation — the persistent VKVM stream was APPENDED on every recompile (one per heap membership version, e.g. per adaptive recolor) and the old derive DispatchCommands lingered in the pre-pass replay list. Every click permanently rendered the whole scene (and its derive pass) ONE MORE TIME per frame — the staircase-into-diashow degradation on all platforms (hekla-verified: 6 picks 27.7 -> 5.3 ms/frame).\n- [Sg] Heap: dynamic geometry values that FIT the existing allocation re-stage IN PLACE (header count rewritten when it changes) — the select-toggle (full array <-> singleton) never reallocs, no free/alloc churn, no header re-bake.\n- [Sg] HeapSpike: `dynpick` probe — repeated adaptive recolors under the two-task picking shape must not accumulate per-frame cost.",
